# A long unattended walk, to fill logs/errors.log.
#
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/explore.keys 1
#
# This is the point of the headless backend. The best defect finder this
# project has is a play session that reaches unusual game states and lets
# Error() record what it did not like; before this, that needed a person.
#
# The walk is deliberately undirected: long runs in one of the eight
# directions, with a search, a rest, a pick-up, a try at the stairs and an ESC
# mixed in. Walking into rock still spends a turn, so the monsters still move
# and their AI still runs -- which is where the out-of-bounds map reads that
# filled the log 343 times in 13 seconds were found. ESC appears regularly so
# that a command which unexpectedly opens a menu cannot swallow the rest of
# the script.
#
# Generated with a seed of 20260814. NOT regenerable: the generator is lost.
#
# This header used to say "the generator is quoted in the commit that added
# this file". It is not. The adding commit is 058ba87, its body quotes no
# generator, and no commit in the history does (checked 2026-08-17 with
# git log --format=%B). Seven key scripts chained their provenance to that
# sentence. Treat this file as the artefact itself: edit it directly, or write
# a new generator and say so here. Tracked as inc-buq.

@include chargen.keys

@dump:arrival

END*5 UP*3 UP*5 ESC PGUP*6 s DOWN*1 > LEFT*3 .*3
UP*2 LEFT*6 ESC UP*2 LEFT*6 g RIGHT*4 s PGUP*5 UP*6
